Run records of codegen/c/viewbinding_test.go's tests that build a program with clang flags
of their own and run it, written by tackc's porttest/rungen and completed
by tools/corpus --update; see tools/corpus/runs.tck for the format.
-- view-bindings-example-is-sanitizer-clean/record --
replaces codegen/c/viewbinding_test.go TestViewBindingsExampleIsSanitizerClean/-O0
replaces codegen/c/viewbinding_test.go TestViewBindingsExampleIsSanitizerClean/-O2
strict-libs the test compiles its build's C with -std=c11 -Wall -Wextra -Werror -fstrict-flex-arrays=3 at its level and flags itself, which the driver's -w turns off; the runner compiles it so
dir examples/view-bindings
opt 0 2
cflags -fstrict-flex-arrays=3 -fsanitize=address,undefined -fsanitize-address-use-after-return=always -fno-sanitize-recover=all -D_DEFAULT_SOURCE -fno-sanitize-address-globals-dead-stripping -ffinite-loops -mllvm -indvars-predicate-loops=true
lacks stdout "FAIL"
count stdout 6 " ok\n"
exit 0
stdout "a view through a pattern binding ok\n"
stdout "a view call written as a statement ok\n"
stdout "a view through a range binding ok\n"
stdout "a view through both ok\n"
stdout "a view of an array payload in a list ok\n"
stdout "a view through a call given a binding ok\n"
stderr ""
